  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: Shell and tube heat exchangers function by passing a hot fluid through
    a cold fluid. There are two inlets and two outlets where each of the fluids gets
    in motion at their respective inlet and gets out of the heat exchanger at their
    outlets. Hot fluid enters through the tube and is heated by conductive heating
    in the tubes. Baffles that direct the flow in the shell create turbulence which
    helps to increase the heat transfer rate and avoids fouling in the tubes and
    shell walls. Let us understand the working of a shell and tube heat exchanger.
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e63ac0177aeed334f9a24408402d8fb6, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 1749380657243123591, guid: e63ac0177aeed334f9a24408402d8fb6,
